es are put through their final trials. But when the player arrives to complete their initiation, they find the place overrun: the demonic Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon has seized the Battlespire, slaughtering its instructors and students and turning it into a staging ground for an invasion of the mortal world of Tamriel. Stranded and alone, the apprentice must fight through the corrupted halls of the Battlespire and venture into the twisted planes of Oblivion beyond. Battling monstrous foes, solving arcane puzzles, and uncovering the scope of Dagon's scheme, the lone survivor becomes the last hope of stopping the Daedric Prince before his armies can spill through into Tamriel and lay waste to the realm.", "summary": "An Elder Scrolls Legend: Battlespire is an action role-playing open world video game developed and published by Bethesda Softworks, set in the world of The Elder Scrolls.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}, {"id": 17, "name": "Fantasy"}, {"id": 38, "name": "Open world"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/an-elder-scrolls-legend-battlespire", "collections": [{"id": 6, "name": "The Elder Scrolls"}]}